# tools/ales_limit_witness.rish — a peak limiter: a hard ceiling the signal may touch yet never cross (ALES49).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES49.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260814/20260814-170815_fill-ales49-lotus-peak-limiter.md
# Stands on: lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 — the Clip, sample_min/sample_max, the range law shape); rests beside the whole
# EQ family (ALES40–48, ALES48's bell re-proven below) without disturbing it.
#
# lotus/limit.rye passes a sample within the ceiling byte-for-byte and pins a louder sample to sign(x)·ceil. The selftest proves:
# silence stays silence; below the ceiling is the identity; a signal pinning both rails limits so no output crosses the ceiling and
# every sign is held; a ceiling at sample_max is the identity for in-range audio; a zero ceiling refuses BadCeiling, an over-rail
# ceiling BadCeiling, an out-of-range span BadRange. Purely local — no network, no keys, no funds, no real device, no sample rate.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/ales_limit_witness.rish

say "ales-limit: Language EN — ALES49 opens the DYNAMICS family: a peak limiter, a hard ceiling the signal may touch yet never cross. Where the fixed-EQ family (ALES40–48) turns frequency, dynamics turns level — a limiter stands between a master and a blown speaker, between a loud take and a clipped file."
say "ales-limit: Style Radiant — the law is stated positively: below the ceiling is the identity (a signal whose peaks all sit within the ceiling passes untouched), and above it every sample is pinned to sign(x)·ceil so the ceiling is never crossed and the sign is always held — the magnitude only ever shrinks."
say "ales-limit: Lens TAME — bounded Clip, u32 span, i16 samples; the ceiling checked as a legal magnitude in [1, sample_max] before any write (a zero ceiling refuses BadCeiling, an over-rail ceiling BadCeiling), an out-of-range span refuses BadRange; one comparison and at most one sign-carry per sample, nothing on the audio path can overflow since a limited magnitude is min(|x|, ceil) <= i16; siloed to lotus/, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no sample rate."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/limit"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/limit.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-limit: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/limit.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-limit: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-limit: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-limit' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-limit: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-limit line"

# The dynamics opener rests beside the finished EQ family — re-prove ALES48's bell still stands green, so nothing regressed.
let bell = run ["sh" "-c" "env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/bell.rye -femit-bin=lotus/bin/bell && lotus/bin/bell selftest 2>&1 | grep -q 'GREEN ales-bell' && echo yes"]
assert (trim bell.out) == "yes" else "ales-limit: the ALES48 parametric-bell witness regressed under the limiter"

say "ales-limit: GREEN — a peak limiter holds a hard ceiling the signal may touch yet never cross; below the ceiling is the identity byte-for-byte, above it every sample is pinned to sign(x)·ceil so the ceiling is never crossed and the sign is always held; a ceiling at sample_max is the identity for in-range audio; a zero ceiling refuses BadCeiling, an over-rail ceiling BadCeiling, an out-of-range span BadRange, each leaving the clip untouched; the ALES48 bell selftest stays GREEN. The fixed-EQ family turned frequency; dynamics now turns level — the next Lotus rung can soften the brickwall with a ratio (a compressor), invert its threshold (a gate), or give it an attack and release over a real time base."
